==================== Branch work276, patch #1 ====================

Add extra debug support.

This patch adds debug switches -mdebug=extra1 through -mdebug=extra4.

This patch also adds the ability to provide a number in the range of -128
through 127 as a debug argument.

The patch also prints additional information about the various floating
point formats used for the different modes.

2026-11-19  Michael Meissner  <meissner@linux.ibm.com>

gcc/

	* gcc/common/config/rs6000/rs6000-common.cc (rs6000_handle_option): Add
	-mdebug=extra{1,2,3,4} and -mdebug=<n>.
	* config/rs6000/rs6000.cc (DEBUG_FMT_ID): New macro.
	(rs6000_debug_fp_mode): New debug function.
	(rs6000_debug_reg_global): If -mdebug=reg, print which -mdebug options
	are set and print extra information about the various floating point
	formats used.
	* config/rs6000/rs6000.h (MASK_DEBUG_*): Add -mdebug=<xxx> options.
	(TARGET_DEBUG_*): Likewise.

